Rule 1 (Input tensor must have a numeric data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 2 (tensor must not be boolean and all dimensions must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor must be of floating-point data type and non-empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 6 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (input tensor must have an integer data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5
>>
Rule 5 (input tensor must have a complex floating-point data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10
>>
Rule 6 (for uint8 tensor, elements must not exceed 15 to prevent overflow when squared)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then max(v_1) ≤ 15
>>
Rule 7 (2-dimensional square matrix tensor with positive dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1) ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 8 (input tensor must have a single or double precision floating-point data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8
